WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.175
Welcome to Part 2 of the deeper dive on
attribute-driven migration to Entra ID.

2
00:00:05.175 --> 00:00:10.260
This series goes below the technical deep
dive, down to the rule text, the commands,

3
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.737
the input files and the failing checks
an engineer actually works with.

4
00:00:14.737 --> 00:00:19.875
Part 1 covered Gates 0 to 3: reading
the organizational unit (OU) tree,

5
00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:26.226
fixing the schema and slots, proving the
attributes, and mapping them through sync.

6
00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.525
This part covers Gates 4 to 6.

7
00:00:28.525 --> 00:00:32.072
That's the dynamic group library
and administrative units,

8
00:00:32.072 --> 00:00:35.402
the Conditional Access
personas and device targeting,

9
00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:39.238
moving Group Policy for devices
and servers, and the PIV binding.

10
00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.507
Facts are as the workbook states them,

11
00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:45.460
design guidance is labeled, and
beta features carry their stage.
